  "Shared: that ChurchCRM was installed or upgraded and whether it worked, a once-a-day check-in while it is in use, the version number, your country, and the type of database. A random installation ID counts each install once.": "",
  "Understand database compatibility": "",
  "Your choice is asked once. You can change it at any time. With No thanks, only a failed install or upgrade is reported.": "",
  "Your data is yours. Install shares only installation and upgrade results, installation ID, software version, installation profile, configured country, and database engine and major/minor version. Errors adds warnings and error details. Full adds page views. None sends only failed installs and upgrades. No level sends your web address or server name. Test installations send nothing. Telemetry is sent to PostHog in the United States.": "",
  "Your data is yours. This reports on the software, never on your church or its people.": "",
  "Your data is yours. To count installs, ChurchCRM reports that it was installed or upgraded and whether that worked, a once-a-day check-in while it is in use, plus the version number, your country, the type of database, and a random installation ID. It never reports member, giving, or other church records, your church name, your web address or server name, or email addresses. You can turn this off at any time in Admin → Telemetry; a failed install or upgrade is still reported. Warnings, error details, and page views are only shared if you choose.": ""
